From: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: reach the BSS fallback when survey is unsupported

Treat -EOPNOTSUPP from get_survey as non-fatal so drivers that support
software scans but expose no survey callback, such as the RTL AX AP
driver, can still run ACS through the existing BSS-based fallback.
Other survey errors stay fatal.

Signed-off-by: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/src/ap/acs.c
+++ b/src/ap/acs.c
@@ -1367,7 +1367,10 @@ static void acs_scan_complete(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 		   iface->conf->acs_num_scans);
 
 	err = hostapd_drv_get_survey(iface->bss[0], 0);
-	if (err) {
+	if (err == -EOPNOTSUPP) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "ACS: Survey unavailable, using BSS-based fallback");
+	} else if (err) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "ACS: Failed to get survey data");
 		goto fail;
 	}
